This directory holds all of the scripts related to the hubSpace hub upload feature.

The main components are:
tusd/ - holds everything run by admins to have the file transfer daemon
    running, including cleaning up stale files. These are cronjobs run by the
    admins, so don't modify them without also changing the copy the admins
    run. Note there are copies for both hgwdev and the hubspace machine.

measure/ - the scripts that measure the state of the hubspace file system and
    output stats for viewing over time
    measureHubSpace.sh - production copy, run as qateam on the hubspace machine,
        writes /home/qateam/hubSpace/YYYY/MM/YYYY-MM-DDTHH.txt.  The hgwdev
        wrapper copies these to /hive/users/qateam/hubSpace/hubspace/YYYY/MM/
    measureHubSpace.dev.sh - hgwdev copy, writes
        /hive/users/qateam/hubSpace/hgwdev/YYYY/MM/YYYY-MM-DDTHH.txt
        The two files are identical, the script picks its data directory
        from the host name.  Keep them in sync.
    hubSpaceReport.py - reads all of those dated reports and writes one HTML
        page of charts (storage, files and users over time, storage by file
        format) for management.  Usage:
            hubSpaceReport.py [-l label] logDir outFile.html
    hubSpaceReport.css, hubSpaceReport.js - the styles and drawing code shared
        by every page hubSpaceReport.py writes.  The pages load them from their
        own directory, so "make install" puts them next to the pages.
    measureHubSpaceWrapper*.bash - the weekly cron wrappers, one per machine.
        The hubspace wrapper only runs the measure script.  The hgwdev wrapper
        runs the measure script, copies the hubspace machine's reports to
        /hive, then writes both pages:
            /hive/users/qateam/hubSpace/hgwdev.html
            /hive/users/qateam/hubSpace/production.html

Installing:
    make install - copies the hgwdev measure and trash cleaner scripts, css and js into
        /hive/users/qateam/hubSpace/, where the hgwdev cron runs them
    make hubspace - prints the rsync command that copies the hubspace machine
        scripts to qateam@hubspace:/home/qateam/hubSpace/.  It does not run
        it, so the copies there are never overwritten by accident.
